(1)The Purpose of the repository

The primary purpose of this repository is to demonstrate core version control skills using Git and collaborative workflows on GitHub.

(2)The steps used to complete the tutorial

Step 1: Install Git & Set Up GitHub
1.Download & Install Git: Go to git-scm.com and download the version for your OS (Windows, Mac, or Linux). Run the installer using the default settings.
2.Create a GitHub Account: Sign up at github.com.
3.Configure Git Locally: Open your terminal Git Bash (Windows) and introduce yourself to Git

Step 2: Create a Local Git Repository
1.Open your terminal or Git Bash.
2.Create a new folder for your project and navigate into it

Step 3: Add a Classmate as a Collaborator
1.Go to GitHub and click the + icon in the top right  New repository.
2.Name your repository  and click Create repository.
3.Link your local repository to GitHub by copying the commands provided on the page:
4.Add classmate:
1.Inside your GitHub repository page, click Settings (gear icon at the top).
2.Click Collaborators in the left sidebar.
3.Click Add people, type your classmate’s GitHub username or email, and send the invite.
4.Your classmate must check their email or GitHub notifications to accept the invite.

Step 4: Create a New Branch
Create and switch to a new working branch (replace feature-branch with whatever name you like).

Step 5: Add a New File
Create a new file containing your first and last name.

Step 6: Commit the File
Stage the new file and commit it with a clear message.

Step 7: Push the New Branch to GitHub
Push your newly created branch up to your online GitHub repository.

Step 8: Create a Pull Request (PR)
1.Go to your repository page on GitHub. You will see a yellow banner saying your branch has recent pushes.
2.Click the green Compare & pull request button.
3.On the right side of the PR creation screen, look for the Reviewers section.
4.Click the gear icon next to Reviewers to select my classmate's name.
5.Click Create pull request.

Step 9: Wait for Approval
 My classmate needs to go to your PR page, click Files changed, click Review changes, select Approve, and submit their review.
While i wait, this is the perfect time to open their repository and review their pull request for them!

Step 10: Merge the Branch
1.Once my classmate has approved it, go back to your Pull Request on GitHub.
2.Scroll to the bottom of the page and click the green Merge pull request button.
3.Click Confirm merge

